<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1982</h1><p class="ref-lede">1982 in world history: 9 events, 1 birth, 12 deaths and 2 works. 197 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1978">1978</a><a href="/years/1979">1979</a><a href="/years/1980">1980</a><a href="/years/1981">1981</a><a href="/years/1982" aria-current="page">1982</a><a href="/years/1983">1983</a><a href="/years/1984">1984</a><a href="/years/1985">1985</a><a href="/years/1986">1986</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-2">2 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Argentina invades the Falkland Islands</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Argentine forces seized the British-held Falklands, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> claims as the Malvinas. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> sent a naval task force; the ten-week war ended in Argentine surrender and hastened the fall of the junta.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-14">14 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Argentine forces surrender at Port Stanley</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The surrender ended the 74-day Falklands War, in which 649 Argentine and 255 British service personnel died. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>'s military junta fell soon after.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-14">14 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Princess Grace of Monaco dies after a car crash</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Former film star Grace Kelly died a day after her car left a mountain road above Monaco. She had given up Hollywood to marry Prince Rainier III in 1956.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/beirut" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beirut.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-16">16 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Phalangist militia begin the Sabra and Shatila massacre</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Lebanese Christian militiamen entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beirut">Beirut</a>'s Sabra and Shatila refugee camps, in an area under Israeli control, and killed hundreds of Palestinian and Lebanese civilians over two days.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beirut">Beirut</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/wassenaar-agreement" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wassenaar-agreement.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/wassenaar-agreement">Wassenaar Agreement</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Wassenaar Agreement was concluded on 24 November 1982 between Dutch employers' organisations and trade unions, at a time of high unemployment.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/falklands-war">Falklands War</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Falklands War was a ten-week conflict in 1982 between Argentina and the United Kingdom over the Falkland Islands and South Georgia.</p></div></li></ol></section>
